      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Maine?",
      "a": "Maine received $3.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government made 8,152 awards in the state with an average award size of $375K. Annual obligations ranged from $2.4B in FY21 up to $3.9B in FY25 and then to $3.1B in FY26 (partial)."
